# ========================================================================
# 
# This ignore design was made only and ONLY for no-bloat repo architecture,
# and personalized-setup preservation
# 
# Here, we exclude ABSOLUTE HATED files/dirs first (like __pycache__)
# Then, we exclude everything
# Then we include only the INTENDED paths...
# 
# Each path/dir/folder has a .gitignore file, in which we tell git to
# track exact files... So updates/patches dont affect local changes
# and additions or files and folder structures
# 
# IF U ARE CONTRIBUTING AND ADDING A PATH TO ANY .gitignore, 
# THEN MAKE A NEW BRANCH BEFORE PUSHING CODE,
# THIS ENSURES SAFETY AND SECURITY
# 
# Thanx to this design, u can store custom global/system-wide data
# or do experiments while development, or anything u wanna do,
# but it wont get pushed while u commit to remote...
# 
# TO EXCLUDE A PATH/ITEM: <path/name>
# TO INCLUDE A DIR: !<path/name>
# TO INCLUDES FILES IN A DIR: <dir>/.gitignore -> !<item/dir 1> , !<item/dir 2> ...
# 
# this makes sure that only the path and its files are tracked...
# ========================================================================

# 1. Exclude everything first
*
# Allow directory traversal + per-dir .gitignore files
!.gitignore

# 1b. Exclude system-specific hated folders everywhere
# (kept AFTER re-includes so they stay excluded)
local
__pycache__

# ================================
# ======   INCLUDE THESE    ======
# ================================
# NOTE: each dir below has its own .gitignore with explicit !file list.
# Root only un-ignores the dir itself; file decisions live in <dir>/.gitignore
!bin/
!config/
!docs/
!installers/
!patches/
!shell/

# Top-level intended files (explicit)
!ARCHITECTURE.md
!README.md
!install.sh
!update.sh
!os-release
!config.jsonc
!--apps-pkgs--
!--aur-pkgs--
!--bare-pkgs--